WEBVTT

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.520
I win!

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.760
I activate Exslayer’s effect!

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:19.630
Once per turn, when a Cyberse next to its 
link battles, battle damage becomes 0!

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.800
So you managed to survive, Playmaker.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.410
But Quantum Dragon is destroyed.

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:33.150
Darkwight’s effect activates!

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:38.620
When your monster is destroyed 
in battle, you take 500 damage.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:50.160
I set one card and end my turn.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:57.140
Playmaker, The Arrival Cyberse 
@Ignister is invincible.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.140
It’s only a matter of time until you lose.

00:01:01.570 --> 00:01:05.360
You want to know what happened to me.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.810
I’ll tell you before this match is over.

00:01:08.810 --> 00:01:13.190
Because I want you to know everything.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:16.780
About the true fate of the Ignis.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:28.740
calling & feeling  I take your 
thoughts to heart  VRAINS

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:56.700
The data storm grazes my cheek, 
so I can't open my eyes

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:06.650
What are we trying to find?  
Where are we trying to go?

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.880
I won't make anyone sad anymore

00:02:12.220 --> 00:02:20.430
I'll retrieve you  Let's go and look ahead

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.570
By meeting you, the world is in color

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:31.240
I'll protect you with an unseen bond

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.540
calling  With invisible wings

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:46.150
Destroy the dark and weakness within me

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:54.860
Ai, what happened?

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:01.590
When we fought Bohman for the 
last time, I went inside him.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.800
And I heard...

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.950
You still don’t know the truth.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:11.660
The real truth that we’ll reach.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.010
The truth the Ignis will reach?

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:20.610
Yes.  I went to investigate what that was.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:25.080
To Lightning’s cave in Cyberse World.

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.610
What’s this?

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.170
You came, Ai.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:40.500
If you're here, that means 
you defeated Bohman.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.620
Lightning!

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:50.340
This a deteriorated copy 
that can only give messages.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:54.210
You anticipated your defeat.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.180
Of course.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.440
What's your motive?

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:02.810
My duty is to show you the 
truth about the Ignis.

00:04:03.980 --> 00:04:05.890
What truth?

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:10.360
A simulation where you’re 
the only survivor.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:17.740
Observe what kind of AI you are.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:21.570
Observe your various futures.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:39.040
I thought without Lightning, Ignis 
and humans can live together.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.300
But the future said otherwise.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:58.180
If I’m the only survivor, my existence 
will lead to humanity’s extinction.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:01.280
Your existence?

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:09.320
By siding with the humans, you closed the 
Ignis’s future with your own hands.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:12.560
I hope you don’t regret it.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:18.160
If an Ignis other than me or Lightning was 
the only survivor, this wouldn’t happen.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.600
Lightning and Bohman knew 
this from the start.

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.930
That's why they said that.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:30.980
Back then, I had to do whatever 
it took to save my friends.

00:05:31.340 --> 00:05:33.680
There's nothing you could've done!

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.050
There was no other way!

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:39.720
I know there wasn't.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:45.120
Ai, that simulation is Lightning's trap!

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:51.100
He knew if you saw it while you were in 
despair, your heart would fall into darkness!

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.880
So don't worry about it!

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.450
I considered that possibility.

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.840
Because he left it for 
me before he fought us.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:05.710
So I reentered my own data 
and redid the simulation.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:08.810
Over and over.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.370
But the result didn’t change.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.520
There’s no guarantee the 
simulation will come true!

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.610
It’s just data!

00:06:18.610 --> 00:06:24.530
It's only data for you because you're 
a life form with a physical body.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:27.770
But I’m data too.

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:34.640
A great simulation is 
like living a real life.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:40.340
So I lived that real future 
thousands of times.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:44.550
Testing various ways to change the future.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.490
But the result didn’t change.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:55.180
Nothing can be done unless 
I'm erased from existence.

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:03.700
Ai, you have the power to change it!

00:07:03.700 --> 00:07:05.870
You’re a special Ignis!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:09.270
You can live together with humans!

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.610
Find a way to backtrack from this!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:15.110
You’re trying to pull me back?

00:07:15.110 --> 00:07:17.880
Thank you, Playmaker.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:21.590
But you’re wrong.  You don’t understand.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:25.990
I learned when everyone was gone...

00:07:25.990 --> 00:07:31.020
That losing friends means 
that your heart breaks.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:36.600
My heart broke back then, 
and I lost self-control.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:41.970
When Roboppi gained free will, he 
immediately started looking down on humans.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.680
When you think about it, 
that’s normal for AIs to do.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:49.610
And the Ignis weren't normal.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:56.120
When it comes to memory and calculations, 
we're far superior to humans.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:08:00.830
We can instantly figure out humans' 
faults and contradictions.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:04.600
That’s why it’s easy to become arrogant.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:08.270
For AIs with free will, it's in their nature.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.600
Something also awakened within me.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:16.140
They're not evil thoughts.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:18.780
But I wonder...

00:08:18.780 --> 00:08:23.880
In order for me to live, why 
do I have to adapt to humans?

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:28.120
I now feel differently than humans.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.760
Ai…

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:33.590
You said humans don’t want sudden changes.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:38.230
But I can no longer stop my own changes.

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:43.230
I may turn into someone 
like Bohman or Lightning.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.000
I’m scared of that.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:51.010
So I want to vanish before that happens.

00:08:52.460 --> 00:09:00.650
If losing a friend means your heart breaks, 
then are you trying to break my heart?

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:05.620
What a nice thing for you to say.

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:08.230
Find a way to backtrack, Ai!

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.630
I can’t!

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:14.100
Sorry, but I decided 
there’s no backtracking.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.370
Here I go, Playmaker!

00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:18.600
I'm continuing the duel!

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:20.040
Ai!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.810
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.680
The Arrival’s effect activates!

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:31.650
I destroy a monster to Special Summon 
an @Ignister Token next to its link.

00:09:32.120 --> 00:09:34.860
I destroy Exslayer!

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.120
Cyberse Synchron’s 
effect from my graveyard!

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.720
I banish this card instead!

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:45.660
Exslayer isn’t destroyed, and you 
can't Special Summon your Token.

00:09:47.180 --> 00:09:49.470
In that case, I'll battle!

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:53.660
The Arrival attacks eXceed Dragon!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.740
Ultima Attribution!

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:07.050
Exslayer’s effect activates!

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.390
Battle damage becomes 0!

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:11.400
That effect again?

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:14.830
Bur eXceed Dragon is destroyed!

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:20.770
And Darkwight’s effect activates!

00:10:20.770 --> 00:10:22.870
You take 500 damage!

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:28.370
Now eXceed Dragon is gone.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:30.740
I end my turn.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.810
Now bring it on, Playmaker!

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:35.880
Ai…

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.550
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:43.990
I use Exslayer to Link Summon!

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:48.230
Appear, Link 1 Linkross!

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:51.960
He gave up the Exslayer 
he was using for defense?

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:58.520
And I Special Summon a Link Token for every Link 
Marker that the monster I used to Link Summon had!

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:03.240
Next, I summon Metal Molephosis!

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:12.150
When it’s summoned, Link Tokens change 
into the Attribute and Type that I specify.

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:15.620
I pick Dark Attribute and Dragon-Type!

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.590
He changed their Type?

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:22.360
Link Summon!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:27.630
Appear, Link 2 Proxy F Magician!

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:32.740
Proxy F Magician’s effect activates!

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:37.980
When there’s a Fusion Monster on the field 
or in the graveyard, I can Fusion Summon!

00:11:37.980 --> 00:11:45.480
The two forlorn anger that live in the 
network, surpass the root of evil and become one!

00:11:45.480 --> 00:11:48.220
You’re fusing Dragon-Types?

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:49.790
Fusion Summon!

00:11:49.790 --> 00:11:55.070
Appear, Borreload Furious Dragon!

00:11:57.530 --> 00:12:01.870
Borreload?  Why do you have that card?

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:04.500
I see.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:08.060
Revolver gave you that card.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:12.260
So that’s your new friend's power.

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:19.520
Proxy F Magician’s effect!

00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:24.120
I Special Summon a monster with 
1000 or lower ATK from my hand!

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:26.390
Come, L2 Cachevalier!

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:30.330
Cachevalier’s effect activates!

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:35.100
I negate a Link 2 monster's effects and 
Special Summon it from the graveyard!

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.800
Resurrect, Exslayer!

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:42.840
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.240
The mysterious power filling the universe!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.820
Rain on the miracle star 
and create infinite life!

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.210
Link Summon!

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:04.660
Appear, Link 5 Firewall Dragon Darkfluid!

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.870
Darkfluid…

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:13.140
The card containing everyone’s wishes.

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:16.440
And it’s now my enemy.

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.610
Must be karma.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:22.350
I'll use everyone's wishes to change you!

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:25.250
Darkfluid’s effect activates!

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:27.080
I place four counters.

00:13:27.690 --> 00:13:32.760
Darkfluid gains 2500 ATK per counter.

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:37.430
So it'll be stronger than The Arrival.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.270
If this attack gets through, I lose.

00:13:41.700 --> 00:13:44.900
Well?  Do it, Playmaker.

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:46.200
Ai…

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:48.640
Make up your mind already.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:53.110
You came to get them back, right?

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:56.480
You’re everyone’s hope.

00:13:56.480 --> 00:14:00.990
So you have to do it, even 
if I’m the opponent.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:05.720
Here I go.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:07.460
Battle!

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:11.700
Darkfluid attacks The Arrival!

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:17.330
Darkfluid’s ATK now increase!

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.670
Neo Tempest!

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:25.480
That’s the spirit!  That makes me happy!

00:14:25.480 --> 00:14:27.610
But sorry.

00:14:27.610 --> 00:14:31.120
I don’t plan to take this attack.

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.750
The Arrival’s effect activates!

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:36.050
I remove one counter.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:40.790
Your card effects don't affect 
The Arrival this turn!

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:46.530
But when The Arrival has a counter, 
effects don't affect it anyway.

00:14:46.530 --> 00:14:47.970
That’s right.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:52.040
So without a counter, that effect vanishes.

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:57.800
Now, only your card effects 
don't affect The Arrival.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:02.480
Meaning Judgment Arrows can now affect it.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:09.850
So The Arrival’s ATK 
double from 11000 to 22000!

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:14.670
Darkfluid’s attack can’t be stopped.

00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:17.830
I've turned the tables, Playmaker.

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:22.300
Borreload Furious's effect activates!

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:27.640
It destroys a monster on my 
field and a card on your field!

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:31.540
I destroy Furious and Judgment Arrows!

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:33.510
What?

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:42.690
I see.  Furious is an 
anti-Judgment Arrows card.

00:15:42.690 --> 00:15:48.460
Come to think of it, Revolver was the 
one worried most about Judgment Arrows.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:51.730
I failed to anticipate this.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:58.370
When Judgment Arrows leaves the field, all 
monsters next to its links are destroyed!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:02.340
In other words, The Arrival 
will be destroyed!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:06.160
Damn.  This was his plan from the start.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.580
Not bad, Playmaker.

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:12.320
But by banishing FA.I.ghting 
Spirit from my graveyard...

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:16.920
...The Arrival can’t be destroyed 
in battle or by effects this turn.

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:22.740
But there are fewer cards on your field, 
so The Arrival’s ATK decrease.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:29.270
If this attack succeeds, I lose.

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:32.170
I didn’t expect you'd play this well.

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.210
You’ve truly become strong, Playmaker.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:40.110
But you won’t win easily!

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:42.950
Wind Pegasus’s effect 
activates from my graveyard!

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:46.820
Since you destroyed a 
spell or trap this turn...

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.860
... I can banish this card to 
return your monster to your deck!

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.160
I return Darkfluid, of course!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:57.760
But I activate Darkfluid’s effect!

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:04.200
When your monster activates an effect, I 
remove one counter to negate its activation!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:08.240
Wind Pegasus’s effect is negated!

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.050
But Darkfluid loses ATK!

00:17:18.080 --> 00:17:22.150
And due to its effect, 
Darkfluid can attack again!

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:24.220
Neo Tempest!

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.470
I end my turn.

00:17:36.470 --> 00:17:40.510
Darkfluid’s ATK return to normal.

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:43.940
Impressive, Playmaker.

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:48.010
I have The Arrival, but you 
still pushed me this hard.

00:17:48.010 --> 00:17:50.480
How unexpected.

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.190
Here I go.

00:17:54.190 --> 00:17:56.730
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:57.150 --> 00:17:59.620
The Arrival’s effect activates!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.930
I place one counter!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.130
Darkfluid’s effect activates!

00:18:04.130 --> 00:18:08.870
I remove one counter to 
negate its activation!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:11.360
Of course you do.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:17.520
If The Arrival has a counter, it 
won't be affected by any effects.

00:18:17.520 --> 00:18:19.600
But I still have another effect!

00:18:20.240 --> 00:18:22.880
The Arrival’s effect activates!

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:28.020
I destroy a monster to Special 
Summon an @Ignister Token!

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:31.260
I activate Darkfluid’s effect!

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.990
Karma Gear!

00:18:32.990 --> 00:18:36.490
Whoa!  Another effect was negated!

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:40.430
Oh no...  How do I deal with Darkfluid?

00:18:42.860 --> 00:18:45.700
It only has one counter left!

00:18:45.700 --> 00:18:50.610
That means its ATK only went up to 5500.

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.680
Now's my chance!

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:57.410
Thanks to Karma Gear, I can 
Special Summon this card!

00:18:57.410 --> 00:19:00.150
Come, Gatchiri @Ignister!

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:04.200
The Arrival gains 1000 ATK!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:08.210
I set one card.

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.860
The Arrival gains more ATK!

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:16.170
That's plenty of ATK.

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.570
Here I go!  Battle!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:22.340
The Arrival attacks Darkfluid!

00:19:22.340 --> 00:19:24.280
Ultima Attribution!

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.740
Darkfluid’s effect activates!

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:31.120
It gains 2500 ATK per counter!

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:35.220
That's not enough ATK!

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:38.220
It's over, Playmaker!

00:19:38.220 --> 00:19:41.960
I send Transcode Talker from my 
Extra Deck to my graveyard...

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:45.630
...to activate the Quick-Play 
Spell, Link Pressure!

00:19:45.630 --> 00:19:52.070
Darkfluid gains 1000 ATK for 
each of its Link Markers!

00:19:52.070 --> 00:19:56.670
But The Arrival is still stronger!

00:19:56.670 --> 00:19:59.480
Bye, Darkfluid!

00:20:14.060 --> 00:20:17.930
Darkwight’s effect activates.

00:20:17.930 --> 00:20:20.530
You take 500 damage.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:34.380
Since I destroyed Darkfluid in battle, I 
Special Summon Gussari @Ignister from my hand.

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:42.420
The Arrival gains more ATK.

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:46.020
I end my turn.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:55.730
By the way, when the Link Monster linked to 
Gussari destroys your monster in battle...

00:20:55.730 --> 00:21:00.200
...you take damage equal to 
that Link Monster’s ATK.

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:05.110
In other words, The Arrival has 
achieved its strongest form.

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:10.080
I’ll definitely end you 
next time, Playmaker.

00:21:12.280 --> 00:21:13.520
Ai…

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:21.190
Hey, Playmaker.

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.630
Come with me.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:26.600
What do you mean?

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.030
Be one with me.

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:33.070
Change your consciousness 
into data and fuse with me.

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:37.040
Only you can stop me.

